	(footprint "eSIM_MFF2_VFDFPN8"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "e6ecdf7c-a9fb-5688-b721-1a7d47a20a35")
		(at 65.5 50.5)
		(descr "MFF2 soldered eSIM, VFDFPN-8 5.0 x 6.0 x 0.9 mm. DERIVED FOOTPRINT (F-17) - not from easyeda2kicad, because MFF2 is a standard package site rather than one LCSC part. Land pattern is the vendor-consensus land published IDENTICALLY by four independent documents covering three silicon vendors: Infineon OPTIGA Connect IoT datasheet rev 3.0 2022-02-18 fig 6 p.22 (md5 eed84276d38b692e2fcfe740b4a94b29); Velocity IoT VIoT-Flex MFF2 p.4; 1NCE IoT SIM Chip Industrial footprint drawing; ConnectedYou CY SIM MFF2 Packaging v1.1/v1.2 section 4 p.5. Pin mapping cross-checked against the normative ETSI TS 102 671 V12.0.0 2018-07 table 6.1 p.13 (md5 b6c0feffce862e5cb98aacb20a67d5a3): pin 1-8 = contacts C5,C6,C7,C8,C4,C3,C2,C1. Pitch axis runs along the 5.0 mm body axis. Pin 1 = bottom-left viewed from top. Exposed pad tied to GND per Infineon table 10 note p.24; numbered 1 so it merges with the GND pin without needing a 9-pin symbol. ETSI annex A publishes a DIFFERENT, socket-compatible land (0.50 x 0.96 at +/-2.675, insulated centre anchors) - deliberately NOT used, see design-log F-17.")
